# The build context for infra/docker/Dockerfile (Issue 10), which every build sends from the repo
# root. An allowlist: nothing enters the context unless it is named here, so a new file (above all
# a .env holding secrets) cannot reach a build daemon, a cache or a layer by accident. Add a line
# here when the Dockerfile starts copying something new; the build fails loudly until you do.
#
# This file lives at the repo root, not under infra/docker/: Docker reads .dockerignore only from
# the root of the build context (docs/IDE/RULES/infra-layout.mdc).

**

!requirements.txt
!src/
!alembic/
!alembic.ini
!scripts/__init__.py
!scripts/db/
!scripts/check_config.py

# Never bytecode, whatever the folders above hold.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
